cache:query:god's actions
$790
God is described as the creator and caretaker of all living things. He created the great whales, every sea creature and every winged bird, declared them good, blessed them and commanded them “to increase and multiply, and fill the waters of the sea… let the birds be multiplied upon the earth”【chunk-9】. He also spoke, “Let the earth bring forth the living creature… cattle and creeping things, and beasts of the earth,” and then made those beasts, cattle and all crawling creatures “according to their kinds,” again seeing his work as good【chunk-10】. The text also uses the phrase “it repented him… that he had made man on the earth” as a figurative way to stress the seriousness of human sin, not a literal change of mind on God’s part【chunk-69】.
$4
