cache:query:Is God considered a man according to the theological perspective that defines a man as a being created in God's image, possessing a spiritual soul with understanding and free will?
$214
No. In that theological view man is defined as the creature “created in God’s image,” the image residing in the soul with understanding and free will, but God Himself is not described as a man [chunk-12].
